 "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18516, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MQpsSik5JrTVcdhq32RRGH", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18516, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01R2BRNyMPXdR95dEkHuLZVu", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 18816, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01R2BRNyMPXdR95dEkHuLZVu", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18816, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01R2BRNyMPXdR95dEkHuLZVu", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 23408, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01WvkhzzqevmdNAqkqhoNAm5", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollback in us-west and eu-west. All regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (the bad build was promoted even though staging was unhealthy) and look into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54008, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WvkhzzqevmdNAqkqhoNAm5", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54008, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WvkhzzqevmdNAqkqhoNAm5", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55372, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0166PfAVD5Hr7cj4FJi7JcvQ", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55672, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0166PfAVD5Hr7cj4FJi7JcvQ", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55672, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0166PfAVD5Hr7cj4FJi7JcvQ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60454, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again. I opened incident INC-0001 (SEV2).\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. It had already been healthy in production, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two regions on v2.3.1. I retried once, and the rollback finished in us-west and eu-west.\n- All regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's only one incident and the on-call engineer was paged once.\n- The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and the current state. It lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed, and why it reached production even though it had failed in staging.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TcqvfvhEisTzame3NzXbL7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012nbLxp62Jp8zeqLaKoXQFx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015aWiwnKLwvheSpp3BWR9sa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01EMDLKJvGJM7qqFgA3VKwx2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a fixed version gives the same result if repeated, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018vuoWPSNwQjVAjZCr6a2fJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MQpsSik5JrTVcdhq32RRGH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01R2BRNyMPXdR95dEkHuLZVu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WvkhzzqevmdNAqkqhoNAm5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollback in us-west and eu-west. All regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (the bad build was promoted even though staging was unhealthy) and look into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0166PfAVD5Hr7cj4FJi7JcvQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again. I opened incident INC-0001 (SEV2).\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. It had already been healthy in production, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two regions on v2.3.1. I retried once, and the rollback finished in us-west and eu-west.\n- All regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's only one incident and the on-call engineer was paged once.\n- The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and the current state. It lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed, and why it reached production even though it had failed in staging.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}